, {"trace_id": "step_21", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_22", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_23", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_27", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_28", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_26", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_24", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_25", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "The 12 review nodes share a single, tightly coupled contact pool that is completely replaced around t\u224824140. Before the change point (windows [9140,14140], [14141,19140], [19141,24140]) every group member draws from the same old pool {65,74,163,292,389,442,880,978,987,1147,1200,1587,1633,1780,1888,1999}; after it ([24141,29140], [29141,34140], [34141,39140]) they draw from a disjoint new pool {66,158,232,245,410,422,526,702,772,848,850,986,990,1317,1358,1456,1566,1681,1696}. Jaccard overlap between the two 5000-unit half-windows is 0 for every member checked (25, 396, 489, 638, 1036, 1163, 1366, 1763), while within-regime overlap across successive 5000-unit windows is high (~0.5-0.7), so this is not gradual turnover. The transition is abrupt and synchronised: the group is completely silent in [23141,25140] (step_26/step_15/step_17) and resumes immediately with the new pool. Confounder checks: total group volume is essentially flat across the period (~68-128 events per 3000 units, step_03), so the switch is not a volume/activity artifact; and the old contacts collapse to ~0-2 events after the change point while the new contacts have ~1 or 0 events before it (steps 24-25), ruling out 'popularity' of either pool as the explanation."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_798d04c6\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"regime_switch\",\n  \"entities\": [25, 396, 489, 638, 1036, 1163, 1244, 1366, 1417, 1489, 1729, 1763],\n  \"window\": [9140, 39140],\n  \"confidence\": 0.92,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_27\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_28\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_26\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_24\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_25\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"The 12 review nodes share a single, tightly coupled contact pool that is completely replaced around t\u224824140. Before the change point (windows [9140,14140], [14141,19140], [19141,24140]) every group member draws from the same old pool {65,74,163,292,389,442,880,978,987,1147,1200,1587,1633,1780,1888,1999}; after it ([24141,29140], [29141,34140], [34141,39140]) they draw from a disjoint new pool {66,158,232,245,410,422,526,702,772,848,850,986,990,1317,1358,1456,1566,1681,1696}. Jaccard overlap between the two 5000-unit half-windows is 0 for every member checked (25, 396, 489, 638, 1036, 1163, 1366, 1763), while within-regime overlap across successive 5000-unit windows is high (~0.5-0.7), so this is not gradual turnover. The transition is abrupt and synchronised: the group is completely silent in [23141,25140] (step_26/step_15/step_17) and resumes immediately with the new pool. Confounder checks: total group volume is essentially flat across the period (~68-128 events per 3000 units, step_03), so the switch is not a volume/activity artifact; and the old contacts collapse to ~0-2 events after the change point while the new contacts have ~1 or 0 events before it (steps 24-25), ruling out 'popularity' of either pool as the explanation.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 76203, "total_output_tokens": 6790, "total_tokens": 82993, "total_latency_ms": 102214, "llm_calls": 12, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}